A goal without a number and a date is just a wish. Compare:

- ❌ "I want to save more money."
- ✅ "I want to save $1,000 for an emergency fund in the next 6 months."

Good financial goals are **specific** (a clear target), **measurable** (a number), and **time-bound** (a deadline). This makes it possible to track progress and know when you''ve actually succeeded.', 1);
